From 305e34c603d30da49c802af58de7f1e02efb17ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "muhammad.alhaddadi@fastbundle.co" <muhammad.alhaddadi@fastbundle.co>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:54:57 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add MonOrm contenders (Python asyncio and Node.js)

_monorm/queries.py and _monorm/index.mjs run the 7 IMDBench queries
with load() and the expression API, on the tables of the _postgres load.
schema.prisma maps the models to those tables, and both languages read it.
The MonOrm import is in one place per language (_orm.py, orm.mjs).
MonOrm has no avg() in load(), split_part or random(): a select() gives the
average ratings, setup uses replace, and ids are sampled in the host language.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
