@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# MonOrm contenders
+
+This folder holds two contenders for IMDBench: MonOrm (Python, asyncio) and MonOrm (Node.js).
+Both run the 7 IMDBench queries on the Postgres tables that `make load-postgres` creates.
+They read the models from one file, `schema.prisma`, which maps to the same tables (`@@map`).
+
+## Notice
+
+This folder is a change to IMDBench (`geldata/imdbench`, Apache-2.0).
+The `LICENSE` file of IMDBench stays as it is.
+Our changes to the upstream files:
+
+- `_shared.py`: the `monorm` and `monorm_js` entries.
+- `jsbench.js`: the `monorm_js` choice, its `getApp` branch and its close call.
+- `Makefile`: the `load-monorm` target and `monorm`, `monorm_js` in the `run-js`, `run-py` and `run-orms` lists.
+- New files: everything in `_monorm/`.
+
+No other contender changed.
+
+## Install
+
+MonOrm comes from the local repository `/Users/mha/projects/orm`.
+The Python import is only in `_orm.py`, and the JS import is only in `orm.mjs`.
+
+Python (3.12 or newer, in the IMDBench venv):
+
+```sh
+pip install -r requirements.txt greenlet
+cd /Users/mha/projects/orm/languages/python/packaging/postgres
+maturin build --release -i <venv>/bin/python -o /tmp/monorm-wheels
+pip install --no-deps /tmp/monorm-wheels/orm_native_postgres-*.whl
+pip install --no-deps /Users/mha/projects/orm
+```
+
+The native build takes several minutes.
+`greenlet` is not in `requirements.txt`, but the SQLAlchemy contender needs it.
+
+Node.js (version 20 or newer):
+
+```sh
+cd _monorm && npm install
+```
+
+`package.json` points to `file:/Users/mha/projects/orm/languages/js`.
+Build the Node addon there first (`npm install && npm run build:native`).
+Set `ORM_NATIVE=<path>/orm.node` to choose another addon file.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+make load-monorm
+python bench.py --query get_movie --query insert_movie monorm monorm_js
+```
+
+The connection URL is `postgres://postgres_bench:edgedbbenchmark@<host>:<port>/postgres_bench`, the database of the `_postgres` contenders.
+Set `IMDBENCH_MONORM_URL` to use another URL.
+
+## Differences from the other contenders
+
+- MonOrm cannot take `avg()` in `load()`, so a second `select()` gives the average rating per movie.
+- MonOrm has no `split_part` and no `random()`, so `setup` strips each title suffix with `replace`, and the ids are sampled in the host language.
+- The queries use the expression API only. No query uses raw SQL.
+
+## Check and local run
+
+`tools/` holds scripts for a small local run without Docker:
+
+- `gen_small_dataset.py` writes a small `dataset.json`.
+- `load_local.py` loads it into one local Postgres database (schema `public` for `_postgres`, schema `sa` for SQLAlchemy).
+- `local_patch/sitecustomize.py` points SQLAlchemy to that database (use it with `PYTHONPATH`).
+- `check_results.py` compares the MonOrm results with the SQLAlchemy and Prisma results for the same ids.
+
+```sh
+python _monorm/tools/gen_small_dataset.py
+(cd dataset && python cleandata.py)
+python _monorm/tools/load_local.py --port 55432 --database imdb_bench
+export PYTHONPATH=$PWD/_monorm/tools/local_patch
+export IMDBENCH_MONORM_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:55432/imdb_bench
+export IMDBENCH_CHECK_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:55432/imdb_bench
+python _monorm/tools/check_results.py
+python bench_python.py -C 2 -D 2 --warmup-time 1 --pg-port 55432 monorm sqlalchemy_asyncio
+```
+
+The check prints `RESULT: PASS` when every query agrees.
+It writes test rows and removes them at the end.
+The new ids and the random numbers in names can differ by design.
+The SQLAlchemy `get_user` has no `ORDER BY`, so the check compares its reviews as a set.
+
+`jsbench.js` loads all JS contenders at start.
+For a Prisma and MonOrm JS run, install and build the other JS contenders first, as `make load` does.
+Prisma needs `DATABASE_URL` in the environment.
+The Prisma `insert_movie` and `insert_movie_plus` setup uses MySQL syntax and fails on Postgres.
+
+Timings from such a run are not valid for a comparison.
